WEBVTT

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.660
What?

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.410
Those are people, aren't they?

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.910
They don't look like ghosts.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.380
So we weren't the only ones left in Harajuku.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.130
What?

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.590
Huh?

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.010
Is something wrong?

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.500
Maybe you're tired.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.350
You think so?

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.990
Well, we've been through a lot today.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.070
We should go home for the day.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.640
I didn't realize that many people 
were inside the bubble.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.000
I'm glad everyone's all right.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.510
I thought we'd get Harajuku to ourselves.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.590
Too bad.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.600
Harajuku belongs to you girls, indeed.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.790
What Miss Misa is trying to say is that,

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.840
since you were chosen by the 
Amatsumara to protect Harajuku,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.020
the neighborhood is as good as yours. Yes!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.990
Oh, I see.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.220
It can create weapons and bubbles 
to protect you from missiles.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.180
The Amatsumara are truly amazing!

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.460
<i>As we've been reporting,</i>

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.450
<i>the giant dome that appeared in Harajuku</i>

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.400
I found a station!

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.210
<i>is currently being investigated 
by the IDF science team,</i>

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.430
<i>but the details are still unknown.</i>

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.530
<i>We'll be updating this story 
as we receive more information.</i>

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.290
Details are unknown, huh?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.970
<i>What's happening inside the dome?</i>

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:20.290
One thing I can say is that we'll feel like 
goldfish in a goldfish bowl for a while.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:18.690
<i>All kinds of theories 
are being posted online.</i>

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.870
<i>As there appear to be no transmissions 
coming from inside the dome,</i>

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.870
Someone I know might be around.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.300
I'm going to check out the city.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:26.230
<i>the well-being of the people 
inside is completely unknown.</i>

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.220
Oh, yeah, you do live around here.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.970
I hope you have an emotional reunion.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.380
Actually, I'll go with you.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.150
I don't want to be left behind.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.250
I'd rather stay together, too.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.930
I'll go with you, indeed.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.300
Misa-chan, you wait here.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.690
It could still be dangerous outside.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.980
How disappointing, indeed.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.110
Sorry.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.330
We'll be back soon.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:49.930
Rito-chan, see anyone you know?

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.020
No, I don't see anyone.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.290
There are people around, but it's so quiet.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.140
It doesn't feel like Harajuku.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.140
It's not that surprising, 
considering what happened.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.830
If the situation persists,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.300
it should be easy to 
stand out this Halloween.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.220
Hey, let's go check out Rito-chan's art.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.450
I was really surprised back then.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.690
I was wondering why you suddenly 
got up and left for a while.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.220
Turned out you were painting on a wall.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.650
I suddenly felt inspired to draw.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.760
She looks like a Harajuku girl.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.750
I know. I might be falling in love.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.970
Maybe I'll try painting again.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:40.190
That wall doesn't budge, 
no matter what you do to it.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.390
So we're trapped in here?

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.680
They're talking about the 
bubble, not this wall, right?

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:52.830
Unfortunately, the bubble's the only 
wall anyone's talking about right now.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.270
There's a commotion going 
on near that weird wall.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:57.870
Really? Why?

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:58.610
Not sure.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:01.360
I wonder what happened.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.300
Let's check it out.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.820
Wait! I told you not to leave me behind!

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.410
Hey, what is this?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.340
I want my mom!

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.410
What's the Earth Defense Force doing?

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:15.470
It's like looking at who I was yesterday.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.820
Kotoko, your hands are as warm as a baby's.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.280
I think everyone's anxious.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.320
There's no way to communicate 
with the outside world.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.600
Maybe we trapped them, 
like the fried shrimp said.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.060
But you could say we protected them, too.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.980
What should we do now?

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.400
Is waiting for help our only option?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.570
When you're stranded,

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.820
you're supposed to stay in one place.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:57.410
It's not good to expend your 
energy by moving around.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.260
Stranded, huh?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:03.480
We have electricity, water, and snacks 
here in the middle of Harajuku, though.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.090
Hey, look there.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.430
What's going on?

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.640
They're all laughing.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.970
Okay.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.440
Get in line if you want one.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.150
It's a crêpe shop!

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:21.520
They must be really hard workers to open 
their shop under these circumstances.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.140
It's so good!

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:25.980
I had no idea crêpes were so delicious.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.250
Everyone seems to be enjoying them.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.210
Yeah.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:29.950
Here.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.770
You girls have some, too.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.040
Let's eat!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.580
It's so good!

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.870
The thinness of the pastry that 
requires advanced technique...

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.210
The exquisite sweetness of the whipped cream...

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.630
And the sourness of the strawberries...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.720
It's the perfect crêpe!

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.720
They really are good.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:55.460
Great expressions.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.180
I love seeing those on everyone's faces.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.120
It's a little embarrassing 
to be watched so closely.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.590
I'm so happy!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.310
So, how much?

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.980
Oh, it's fine.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.370
You paid with your smiles.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:10.620
You're such a nice person!

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.780
But why are you handing out 
crêpes at a time like this?

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.360
For free, no less.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.710
Because it's a time like this, I guess.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.690
Everyone's uneasy since the UFOs 
suddenly arrived and Harajuku

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.060
was surrounded by this weird dome.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.870
So I wanted to do something for them.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:31.400
Since I run a crêpe shop, 
this is all I can do, though.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.140
C-C-Crêpes, huh?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.930
I wish I could have had one.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.410
I wanted one, too.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:44.870
If we had internet access, the news 
would've spread in an instant.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.250
Let's go again sometime.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.070
We owe her more than our smiles.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:53.580
Why don't we reopen Park, too?

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.770
What a coincidence.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:57.180
I was just thinking the same thing.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.790
Since we're a pop-up shop, 
it's a waste for us to be closed.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.950
And we may be able to make someone smile.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:04.750
Yeah.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.450
Fantastic!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.760
A rival has inspired you 
to resume creating again!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:15.090
This must be what they call a heated 
development... a passionate story!

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.350
That crêpe shop isn't our rival, though.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:25.020
Oh, right! I've been thinking about the 
Park reopening commemorative menu.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:28.960
I thought we could borrow an idea from 
that apple pie shop that always has a line,

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:35.670
and make something crunchy on the outside, 
but with sweet mousse on the inside.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.820
We could make the colors poppy and cute, too.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:42.780
Sorry, but I was in the 
middle of making clothes.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.400
Rito, the rest is up to you.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.920
Kotoko, let's talk over there.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.380
I'm excited for the reopening, indeed.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.880
Let's watch them work.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:57.420
Pastel colors are popular this year, so...

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.850
Seems like frillier designs 
are more popular right now.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.130
Rito, are you awake?

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:08.690
Huh?

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.280
You haven't moved in a long time.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.670
I don't know what to draw.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.620
How unusual for you to be uninspired.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.750
Want to eat something tasty 
to commemorate your slump?

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:29.300
Statistically speaking, you can't draw 
anything you like when you feel uninspired.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.750
Why don't you relax instead?

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.220
Maybe I'll go for a walk, then.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:42.080
<i>I was so excited about 
reopening Park earlier.</i>

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.780
<i>I wonder why I can't come up with any ideas.</i>

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:57.050
<i>I drew her just because I wanted to.
It didn't take any thought at all.</i>

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:03.320
<i>I wonder what I should draw 
that will make everyone smile.</i>

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:11.890
<i>I've never thought about 
that when drawing before.</i>

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:22.100
Hey!

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.900
What are you doing here?

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:25.770
What's that?

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:27.440
Oh, this?

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:29.730
I'm making deliveries.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.960
You deliver, too?

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.610
You drew this?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.070
That's amazing!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.320
Nah. I just like drawing.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.910
That's important.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:47.600
I love crêpes, too.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:51.630
I like eating them, but I like 
making them even more.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:54.140
You're amazing.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.410
My friends and I were just talking about you.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.850
Oh, those cute eaters?

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:04.220
We're all trapped inside this 
wall and feeling hopeless.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:09.310
It's amazing that you're doing 
something to make everyone smile.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.540
There's nothing amazing about it.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.380
I'm just doing what I want to do.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:18.950
I told you, I like seeing people 
smile while they eat crêpes.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.990
Smile...

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.700
So, Sensei, any plans for your next project?

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.280
Oh, sorry. Should I not have asked?

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:29.000
No, it's okay.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:32.890
I just don't know what to draw.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.980
You mean you can't come up with an idea?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.510
We run a shop, too.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.280
We wanted to do something after seeing you.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.930
So we all started getting things ready,

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:47.960
but when I started wondering what 
would make our customers happy,

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.800
I suddenly couldn't draw anymore.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.730
I see.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.350
Instead of worrying about the tough stuff,

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:57.110
why don't you draw what you want to draw?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.520
By the way, I'm a fan of this drawing!

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.660
Oh, look at the time!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.700
I'm still in the middle of my deliveries.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.540
Sorry for making you listen to me rant.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.110
No, I'm glad we talked.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:13.670
Um...

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.580
I'm Sayumi. What's your name?

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.640
Rito.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.910
I look forward to seeing 
your shop, Rito-chan!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.580
What I want to do...

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:27.570
What I want to draw...

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.180
It's Rito-chan's new work!

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:44.200
I knew there was a reason 
you hadn't come back.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.210
We were waiting so long, I thought 
I'd get stuck to my chair.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.160
Rito-chan, Rito-chan, what's that?

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.860
It's...

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.680
You'll have to wait and see.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.630
By the way, wouldn't you say you 
need two excellent assistants?

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.390
Can I pay you in macarons?

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:02.640
I'm in!

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.650
Make mine banana and soybean flour flavor.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.140
Sounds like something you'd like. Got it.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.670
Does everyone have what they need? Let's go.

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:11.860
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:14.840
Are all artists such slave drivers?

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.410
Misa-chan, that's a lot of pink.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:18.860
Yes, indeed.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.330
I hope we can finish it today.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.440
Rito-chan, you're raring to go!

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.880
I'm excited to see it finished, too.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.170
I'm excited, indeed!

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:30.410
Okay, let's go!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.020
A Scooper!

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:39.290
When did it get here?

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:43.400
There doesn't seem to 
be a hole in the bubble.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:49.300
Maybe it entered when the 
hole opened up last time

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.490
and has been hiding until now.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.270
It should've stayed hidden.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:55.380
Look.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.700
It's coming down.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:01.720
It's headed toward Rito-chan's drawing.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.920
It must be here to steal 
Rito-san's creativity...

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:08.260
In other words, the drawing 
Rito-san made on the wall.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.170
No way! But it's not finished yet.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:15.110
Perhaps it looks finished to them.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:19.460
We can't let it take my—no, our drawing.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:22.110
Thieves must be punished.

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.970
Misa-chan, wait for us at Park.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.880
Good luck, indeed.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.560
Urahara deployed!

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.520
Let's go.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:43.860
Yeah.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.280
There aren't many of them, but be careful.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:51.620
Got it.

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:54.320
By the way, what are the 
residents of Harajuku doing

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:56.310
while the Urahara is deployed?

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.090
Let's see...

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.710
Looks like there's nobody around.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.650
<i>Excuse the interruption.</i>

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:02.830
What?

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:06.130
<i>Since Urahara is a separate 
space from Harajuku,</i>

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.260
<i>your neighbors aren't there. Yes.</i>

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:10.150
Oh, right.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.560
Does that mean, since no one's here,

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.880
I can give them everything 
this thing can muster?

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:20.990
Since these Scoopers are small, unlike 
that big one that turned into popcorn,

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.290
I'll lower the power on your cannon 
and set it to rapid-fire mode.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.980
I'm counting on you to handle that stuff.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.270
This place looks as cheerful as ever.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:37.410
Maybe I'll make a reservation 
at a Halloween zombie party.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:41.100
Kotoko, do you know where the Scoopers went?

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:46.680
<i>There are too many buildings for me 
to see what's happening on the ground.</i>

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:51.530
<i>Hey, that building was remodeled 
recently to build a general store.</i>

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.380
<i>They sell these cute dog mugs...</i>

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.190
Kotoko.

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:57.220
<i>Oh, wait! I'll try changing my search method.</i>

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:00.820
I'm not very good at hide-and-seek.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.390
I don't like sneaking around.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:06.610
I'll stir them up, and you can 
finish them off, just like always.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:08.110
Okay.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:12.130
I don't know where they'll be coming from.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:15.880
It might be good for you to stick 
together and cover each other's backs.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:16.570
Got it.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:20.660
Cover that side.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.410
Is this a big responsibility?

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.610
I know you can handle it. Let's go.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:27.720
There!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.510
Macarons?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.510
Above you!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.590
What a cute color. I'm keeping this one.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:54.820
<i>I changed my search method.</i>

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:59.980
I tried detecting heat, like I 
did with the popcorn Scooper.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:04.830
I found a few objects emitting 
high temperatures in the area.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.600
The principle behind it is...

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.700
You can tell us later.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:08.940
How many are left?

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.400
<i>Two. They're heading toward 
Rito-chan's drawing.</i>

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:13.300
Got it.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:16.720
There they are.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.620
What are they doing?

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:19.500
I don't know.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:22.310
It doesn't look like they're 
searching for a pancake shop.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.520
Trying to steal our drawing?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.400
I won't let you take Rito's drawing!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.580
You can have this instead!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.550
Oh, did I overdo it?

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.270
But that doesn't matter, right?

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:39.980
I'm not detecting anything.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:41.030
Good work.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.870
Here's your reward.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.990
Yay! I got a macaron!

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.900
It tastes like lemons!

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.510
This one's banana and soybean flour!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.930
Huh?

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.890
Those aren't snacks.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.620
I thought that all Scoopers turned into snacks.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:07.330
<i>This must be the effect of the Amatsumara.</i>

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:10.560
<i>Since it turns thoughts into matter, 
it won't always be snacks.</i>

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:13.640
<i>For example, in this case,</i>

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:18.240
<i>maybe something you wanted 
someone to see materialized.</i>

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:22.690
Could someone translate what the shrimp said?

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.180
Ah, excuse me.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:28.400
We won't know unless we ask the Amatsumara.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.060
If you didn't know, you should've said so.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.520
That wasted valuable time.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:42.740
How cute.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.290
Can we take them home?

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:45.970
What?

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.690
Can we?

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:51.960
<i>Since they were created by the 
Amatsumara, it should be fine.</i>

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:51.060
Call In Progress

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.820
Yeah, but we don't know what they are.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:00.030
Shirako, Shirako.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.480
Shirako? Are you called Shirako?

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.710
Shirako, Shirako.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.330
Shirako.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.540
So cute...

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:09.870
I'm taking you home!

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:14.060
Let's take the pigeon Shirako home, too!

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:17.460
Misa-chan's waiting for us. 
Let's head back to the shop first.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.560
It's done.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:35.520
All right!

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:37.740
I helped, indeed.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:41.840
Yes, we couldn't have finished 
it without your help, miss.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:44.320
You were all talk, shrimp.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:47.140
Why did you draw a house?

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:51.040
This is the house I lived in with my 
family before moving in with my grandma.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.750
It's gone now. I was worried I'd 
forget it if I didn't draw it.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.320
It's a lovely house.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:02.680
It'd be great if we all could live in a house 
together someday while running Park.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.720
You'll design it, of course.

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:06.170
Yeah.

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:10.220
Did you make these drawings on the wall?

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.620
I was secretly a fan!

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:14.850
They're cool.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.460
You can take a picture, 
but you can't use SNS, you know.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.150
I'm sure we'll get out of here soon.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.570
Honestly, they haven't a care in the world.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.500
That's just how Harajuku is.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.620
You finished your drawing!

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.710
Sayumi-san.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:31.250
Call me Sayumin.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.340
That's what my friends call me.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.630
Friends...

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:37.590
Glad to know you.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.220
Uh...

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.840
I'm Kotoko!

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.900
Mari. Nice to meet you, Sayumin.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:46.620
Nice to meet you, Kotoko-chan and Mari-chan.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.600
Mari-chan, are you blushing?

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.830
It's a little warm here, isn't it?

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:53.250
The temperature is...

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.720
Kotoko, want some gummies?

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.060
Nice expression.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.320
Thank you, Sayumin.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:07.950
Limited Time Only!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:09.160
There.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.900
Did you come to congratulate me?

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.000
Want some fish sausage?

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.960
Let's open up the shop.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:19.400
Open shop, open shop.

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:20.570
Open shop, open shop.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.160
Open shop.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.730
Now that you're back to your usual self,

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:26.810
we'll have to cancel 
commemorating your slump.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.930
I'm excited, indeed.

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.140
Park's finally reopening.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:35.850
This is a pretty nice display.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.140
Mari-chan!

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:40.320
What?

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:41.370
Huh?

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.250
What?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.320
Huh?

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:52.140
I know I slept last night!

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:27.470
Ice cream is cold and delicious!

00:23:27.470 --> 00:23:29.100
I'd like some, too!

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.410
It's in the freezer.

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:31.840
Oh, this must be it.

00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:33.730
It's rather hard and salty.

00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:35.250
It tastes like tomatoes, too.

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:37.010
That's frozen pizza.
